Senior DevOps / SRE Interview – Uber

Many engineers prepare:

Kubernetes
Terraform
CI/CD
Cloud

But interviews at this level test something very different.

⸻

Round 1 – System Behavior & Edge Cases (45 min)

• Your service works fine at 1k RPS but starts failing at 5k RPS. What changes?
• How do you handle connection exhaustion in a high-traffic microservices system?
• Your cache hit rate drops suddenly after deployment. What could cause this?
• How do you design rate limiting without impacting real users?
• What happens when your message queue starts lagging during peak traffic?

⸻

Round 2 – Failure & Debugging (60 min)

• CPU and memory look normal, but response time increases. Where do you check?
• Traffic is unevenly distributed across pods. Why could this happen?
• One dependency is slow, but not down. How does it affect your system?
• You see intermittent failures only during peak hours. How do you debug?
• Everything is working, but costs suddenly increased 2x. What do you investigate?

⸻

Round 3 – Engineering Judgment (30 min)

• When do you choose consistency over availability?
• How do you decide between vertical scaling vs horizontal scaling?
• When should you NOT use Kubernetes for a system?

⸻

💡 Reality

Senior interviews don’t test:

• commands
• tools
• definitions

They test:

• how systems behave under load
• how failures propagate
• how you make decisions under uncertainty

⸻

That’s where most engineers struggle.

Because they prepare tools…
but not system behavior.
